cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use survfcbf, please cite it as below."
title: "survfcbf: Fast Correlation-Based Filter Feature Selection for Right-Censored Survival Data"
type: software
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.24472789"
authors:
  - family-names: Fernandez-Lozano
    given-names: Carlos
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0003-0413-5677"
    affiliation: "Universidade da Coruña and Institute of Biomedical Research of A Coruña (INIBIC)"
repository-code: "https://github.com/cafernandezlo/survfcbf"
url: "https://github.com/cafernandezlo/survfcbf"
license: GPL-3.0-only
abstract: >-
  Adapts the Fast Correlation-Based Filter (FCBF; Yu and Liu, 2003) to
  right-censored survival data, carrying its approximate Markov blanket
  (predominance) feature pruning to time-to-event outcomes. Provides the
  method together with a leakage-safe nested cross-validation harness, a
  known-truth survival data simulator with cluster-level scoring, and
  wrappers for the standard filter baselines.
keywords:
  - feature selection
  - survival analysis
  - FCBF
  - Markov blanket
  - high-dimensional data
  - R
